               <div class=\"item-title\">\n   678→                            <span class=\"update-product\">Windsurf:</span>\n   679→                            <a href=\"https://codeium.com/windsurf\" target=\"_blank\">MCP Integration</a>\n   680→                        </div>\n   681→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   682→                            MCP integration allows users to enhance AI workflows by connecting to custom tools and services for extended capabilities.\n   683→                        </div>\n   684→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   685→                            April 10, 2026\n   686→                        </div>\n   687→                    </div>\n   688→\n   689→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   690→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   691→                            <span class=\"update-product\">Continue:</span>\n   692→                            <a href=\"https://continue.dev\" target=\"_blank\">Continuous Code Quality</a>\n   693→                        </div>\n   694→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   695→                            Source-controlled AI checks on every pull request, allowing teams to define standards as checks enforced by AI with human oversight.\n   696→                        </div>\n   697→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   698→                            April 10, 2026\n   699→                        </div>\n   700→                    </div>\n   701→\n   702→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   703→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   704→                            <span class=\"update-product\">Claude Code:</span>\n   705→                            <a href=\"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/overview\" target=\"_blank\">Terminal Agentic Tool</a>\n   706→                        </div>\n   707→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   708→                            Terminal-based tool helps developers build features from descriptions, debug issues, navigate codebases, and automate tedious tasks.\n   709→                        </div>\n   710→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   711→                            April 10, 2026\n   712→                        </div>\n   713→                    </div>\n   714→\n   715→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   716→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   717→                            <span class=\"update-product\">Devin:</span>\n   718→                            <a href=\"https://devin.ai\" target=\"_blank\">Nubank Case Study</a>\n   719→                        </div>\n   720→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   721→                            Nubank achieved 8-12x efficiency gains and over 20x cost savings on a major ETL migration project using Devin's AI agents.\n   722→                        </div>\n   723→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   724→                            April 10, 2026\n   725→                        </div>\n   726→                    </div>\n   727→                </div>\n   728→            </section>\n   729→\n   730→            <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n   731→            <section class=\"technical-insights section\">\n   732→                <div class=\"section-header\">\n   733→                    <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   734→                </div>\n   735→                <div class=\"section-content\">\n   736→                    <div class=\"stats-summary\">\n   737→                        <strong>24 insights</strong> from industry experts\n   738→                    </div>\n   739→\n   740→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   741→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   742→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   743→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/24/deepseek-v4/\" target=\"_blank\">DeepSeek V4</a>\n   744→                        </div>\n   745→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   746→                            DeepSeek-V4 with Mixture-of-Experts at fraction of price. 1M token context, MIT license, extremely competitive pricing.\n   747→                        </div>\n   748→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   749→                            Simon Willison • Apr 24\n   750→                        </div>\n   751→                    </div>\n   752→\n   753→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   754→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   755→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   756→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/24/#:~:text=Claude%20Code\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code postmortem</a>\n   757→                        </div>\n   758→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   759→                            Three harness bugs (not model issues) caused Claude Code quality degradation. Cleared thinking repeatedly due to bug.\n   760→                        </div>\n   761→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   762→                            Simon Willison • Apr 24\n   763→                        </div>\n   764→                    </div>\n   765→\n   766→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   767→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   768→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   769→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/copilot-plans/\" target=\"_blank\">Copilot tightening limits</a>\n   770→                        </div>\n   771→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   772→                            \"Agentic workflows have fundamentally changed Copilot's compute demands.\" Single agentic requests burn more tokens cutting margins.\n   773→                        </div>\n   774→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   775→                            Simon Willison • Apr 22\n   776→                        </div>\n   777→                    </div>\n   778→\n   779→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   780→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   781→                            <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   782→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/claude-code-100/\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code $100/month</a>\n   783→                        </div>\n   784→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   785→                            Anthropic quietly added $100/month tier to pricing page then reverted. Unclear if intentional leak or mistake.\n   786→                        </div>\n   787→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   788→                            Simon Willison • Apr 22\n   789→                        </div>\n   790→                    </div>\n   791→\n   792→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   793→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   794→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   795→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/#:~:text=Firefox%20150\" target=\"_blank\">Firefox 150: 271 bugs fixed</a>\n   796→                        </div>\n   797→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   798→                            Mozilla applied Claude Mythos Preview to Firefox, fixing 271 vulnerabilities. CTO: \"Defenders finally have a chance to win.\"\n   799→                        </div>\n   800→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   801→                            Bobby Holley • Apr 22\n   802→                        </div>\n   803→                    </div>\n   804→\n   805→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   806→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   807→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   808→                            <a href=\"https://llm-stats.com/gpt-5-5-vs-claude-opus-4-7\" target=\"_blank\">GPT-5.5 vs Claude Opus 4.7</a>\n   809→                        </div>\n   810→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   811→                            Claude Opus 4.7 leads on 6 of 10 benchmarks, GPT-5.5 on 4. Margins between 2-13 points.\n   812→                        </div>\n   813→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   814→                            Jonathan Chavez • Apr 23\n   815→                        </div>\n   816→                    </div>\n   817→\n   818→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   819→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   820→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   821→                            <a href=\"https://llm-stats.com/gpt-5-5-vs-gpt-5-4\" target=\"_blank\">GPT-5.5 vs GPT-5.4</a>\n   822→                        </div>\n   823→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   824→                            GPT-5.5 delivers 2× per-token price with identical latency, same 1M-token context, improvements on 9 of 10 benchmarks.\n   825→                        </div>\n   826→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   827→                            Jonathan Chavez • Apr 23\n   828→                        </div>\n   829→                    </div>\n   830→\n   831→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   832→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   833→                            <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   834→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/19/headless/\" target=\"_blank\">Headless everything: APIs as UI</a>\n   835→                        </div>\n   836→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   837→                            \"Personal AIs better than services directly; headless services quicker than GUI with bot-controlled mouse.\" Disrupts per-head SaaS pricing.\n   838→                        </div>\n   839→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   840→                            Matt Webb, Benioff • Apr 19\n   841→                        </div>\n   842→                    </div>\n   843→\n   844→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   845→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   846→                            <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   847→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/21/#:~:text=Less%20human%20AI%20agents\" target=\"_blank\">Less human AI agents</a>\n   848→                        </div>\n   849→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   850→                            \"AI agents too human in banal sense: lack stringency, patience, focus. Faced with awkward tasks, drift toward familiar.\"\n   851→                        </div>\n   852→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   853→                            Andreas Påhlsson-Notini • Apr 21\n   854→                        </div>\n   855→                    </div>\n   856→\n   857→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   858→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   859→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   860→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/20/claude-token-counter/\" target=\"_blank\">Claude token inflation</a>\n   861→                        </div>\n   862→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   863→                            Opus 4.7 tokenizer uses 1.46x tokens vs 4.6 for system prompt. Same pricing but ~40% more expensive due to token inflation.\n   864→                        </div>\n   865→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   866→                            Simon Willison • Apr 20\n   867→                        </div>\n   868→                    </div>\n   869→\n   870→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   871→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   872→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   873→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/24/#:~:text=For%20You\" target=\"_blank\">Bluesky feed scaling</a>\n   874→                        </div>\n   875→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   876→                            Serves 72,000 users from single Go process using SQLite on gaming PC. Cost: $30/month total.\n   877→                        </div>\n   878→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   879→                            spacecowboy • Apr 24\n   880→                        </div>\n   881→                    </div>\n   882→\n   883→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   884→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   885→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   886→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/24/#:~:text=honker\" target=\"_blank\">honker: Postgres NOTIFY for SQLite</a>\n   887→                        </div>\n   888→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   889→                            Rust SQLite extension implementing Postgres-style NOTIFY/LISTEN. Queue and stream abstractions with transactional outbox.\n   890→                        </div>\n   891→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   892→                            Russell Romney • Apr 24\n   893→                        </div>\n   894→                    </div>\n   895→\n   896→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   897→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   898→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   899→                            <a href=\"https://llm-stats.com/claude-opus-4-7-vs-opus-4-6\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Opus 4.7 vs 4.6</a>\n   900→                        </div>\n   901→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   902→                            Opus 4.7 wins on 12 of 14 benchmarks at same $5/$25 price. Includes migration checklist.\n   903→                        </div>\n   904→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   905→                            Jonathan Chavez • Apr 17\n   906→                        </div>\n   907→                    </div>\n   908→\n   909→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   910→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   911→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   912→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/18/claude-opus-4-7-system-prompt/\" target=\"_blank\">Opus 4.7 system prompt</a>\n   913→                        </div>\n   914→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   915→                            Anthropic published system prompts for Opus 4.7 and 4.6 - only major AI lab to do so.\n   916→                        </div>\n   917→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   918→                            Simon Willison • Apr 18\n   919→                        </div>\n   920→                    </div>\n   921→\n   922→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   923→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   924→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   925→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/qwen3-6-27b/\" target=\"_blank\">Qwen3.6-27B coding</a>\n   926→                        </div>\n   927→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   928→                            27B dense model claiming flagship-level agentic coding. 55.6GB vs 807GB for 397B-A17B.\n   929→                        </div>\n   930→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   931→                            Simon Willison • Apr 22\n   932→                        </div>\n   933→                    </div>\n   934→\n   935→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   936→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   937→                            <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   938→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/23/gpt-5-5-pelican/\" target=\"_blank\">Testing GPT-5.5</a>\n   939→                        </div>\n   940→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   941→                            \"Fast, effective, highly capable—I ask it to build things and it builds exactly what I ask.\"\n   942→                        </div>\n   943→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   944→                            Simon Willison • Apr 23\n   945→                        </div>\n   946→                    </div>\n   947→\n   948→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   949→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   950→                            <span class=\"insight-type tutorial\">Tutorial</span>\n   951→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/23/extract-pdf-text-liteparse-web/\" target=\"_blank\">LiteParse for the web</a>\n   952→                        </div>\n   953→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   954→                            Browser-based PDF text extraction using LlamaIndex libraries. Runs entirely client-side.\n   955→                        </div>\n   956→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   957→                            Simon Willison • Apr 23\n   958→                        </div>\n   959→                    </div>\n   960→\n   961→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   962→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   963→                            <span class=\"insight-type tutorial\">Tutorial</span>\n   964→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/21/wheres-the-raccoon/\" target=\"_blank\">ChatGPT Images 2.0</a>\n   965→                        </div>\n   966→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   967→                            OpenAI released ChatGPT Images 2.0. Altman: \"Leap from gpt-image-1 to 2 equivalent to GPT-3 to GPT-5.\"\n   968→                        </div>\n   969→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   970→                            Simon Willison • Apr 21\n   971→                        </div>\n   972→                    </div>\n   973→\n   974→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   975→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   976→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   977→                            <a href=\"https://llm-stats.com/ai-news\" target=\"_blank\">LLM News Today</a>\n   978→                        </div>\n   979→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   980→                            Daily aggregation of AI model releases and benchmarks. Tracks 50+ benchmarks across 500+ models.\n   981→                        </div>\n   982→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   983→                            LLM Stats • Apr 21\n   984→                        </div>\n   985→                    </div>\n   986→\n   987→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   988→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   989→                            <span class=\"insight-type tutorial\">Tutorial</span>\n   990→                            <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CsNaJSTJGB4\" target=\"_blank\">AI Coding Models in 2026</a>\n   991→                        </div>\n   992→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   993→                            YouTube covering AI coding models, security (6:53), implementing skills with LLMs, and TDD.\n   994→                        </div>\n   995→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   996→                            YouTube • Apr 18\n   997→                        </div>\n   998→                    </div>\n   999→\n  1000→                    <div class=\"item\">\n  1001→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n  1002→                            <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1003→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/17/pycon-us-2026/\" target=\"_blank\">PyCon US 2026 tracks</a>\n  1004→                        </div>\n  1005→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n  1006→                            PyCon US 2026 features new AI and security tracks. May 13-19 in Long Beach, CA.\n  1007→                        </div>\n  1008→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n  1009→                            Simon Willison • Apr 17\n  1010→                        </div>\n  1011→                    </div>\n  1012→\n  1013→                    <div class=\"item\">\n  1014→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n  1015→                            <span class=\"insight-type tutorial\">Tutorial</span>\n  1016→                            <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Slm-Rns1-RM\" target=\"_blank\">This Week in AI</a>\n  1017→                        </div>\n  1018→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n  1019→                            Weekly rundown of AI news from engineers' perspective. Covers model releases, tools, developer updates.\n  1020→                        </div>\n  1021→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n  1022→                            YouTube • Apr 17\n  1023→                        </div>